Still 1.2.0. The tap is heard now, not felt.

The accelerometer was always the fallback, chosen because iOS exposes one input at a time, and at the 100 Hz it delivers a tap is four samples. A microphone gives forty. On the recording you made with audible taps the new detector finds seven gestures of seven with no false arms; the old one managed five.

While capturing it listens to the helmet, so you can tap the helmet to stop talking. While listening it uses the phone's own.
